+++ b/docs/WIFI_STATION_MANAGER.md
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Native station-management extension
+
+Adds copied station configuration/observations to the existing asynchronous Wi-Fi
+worker in Runtime0.2.19, based on the deployed Runtime0.2.18 source
+8d713b52edca004e1d53bf30a1c584859fe33d14. Old radio/async table prefixes, request,
+progress and lease structures remain unchanged. `RiscWifiStationV1.h` and
+`GardenWifiStationV1.h` append separately size/tag/version-checked capabilities.
+NativeHardware copies the complete outer table instead of advertising a suffix
+beyond a copied prefix.
+
+The existing owner token and worker serialize SDK operations. Detailed scans copy
+BSSID alongside the unchanged old scan record. Station observations contain
+actual AP security/channel/RSSI and interface address/gateway/netmask/DNS. Static
+IPv4 is validated before enqueue and applied with DHCP stopped before station
+start. SDK disconnect reasons distinguish authentication/no-AP/link failure;
+association without address times out as address failure. Link rate is not
+invented from RSSI or advertised protocol flags.
+
+A connected worker accepts repeat scans and Internet probes. Monotonic completion
+revisions distinguish new completions even when the caller misses the intermediate
+RUNNING/CHECKING state. HTTP probes use the fixed Google generate_204 endpoint,
+SDK timeout3000ms, no body/credentials/redirect following. Empty204 is reachable;
+200/redirect is a possible portal; other failure is unverified Internet. The GUI
+never blocks on this operation. Cancel returns pending until the worker finishes
+cleanup. Failed HTTP cleanup retains the worker instead of claiming quiescence.
+
+The production provider/CpuPort/native-worker host suite exercises the real code
+against SDK shims. New cases cover malformed configuration, copied scan/BSSID,
+static-IP/DHCP/DNS call order, authentication, address timeout, repeated connected
+scans, repeated probes, portal/failure/cancel and HTTP-cleanup failure. Existing
+setup/teardown, contention, old-prefix and lease cases remain included. These are
+not physical RF results. Run with WATCH_SOURCE pointing at the matching provider:
+
+```
+WATCH_SOURCE=../Watch bash test/run_radio_async_test.sh
+WATCH_SOURCE=../Watch SANITIZE=1 ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0 bash test/run_radio_async_test.sh
+```
+
+Product firmware assembly must preserve the deployed board/native storage and
+provider selections. A generic SDK-compiled firmware.bin is not an X4 full0x0
+image. No live network or device flashing is part of these tests.
